<!--BlockML Documentation — author semantic structure on imported A03 pages
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_01_AuthorPages-->
<task:A03_01_AuthorPages xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that authors the semantic structure of imported A03 pages
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: enrich every page imported by A03_02_CopyData with
    the semantic scaffold that A04 will render. This task does not copy
    or delete A03 data.

    - **Import** — A03_02_CopyData already wiped A03 data and imported the
      full A02 data tree with packages and names remapped
    - **Identity** — title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType, is stay on
      the imported A03 page
    - **Links** — see / source / Navigation targets may name only A03
      Blocks or lib Blocks from authorativeSources; never a Block from
      another sector
    - **Semantics** — author learningObjectives, readerOutcomes, scopes,
      exclusions, authoritativeSources, and content as a specification
      of what to show, not as finished rendered prose
    - **Template** — org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
      is the structural pattern only, not a domain-content source
    - **Sources** — authorativeSources is BlockMLSourceSet, the same set as
      A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Author the semantic structure that specifies what each imported
          A03 page must show. Sector 3 writes specification, not the
          finished site. Sector 4 (A04_RenderingSector) renders prose,
          examples, and code from that specification.

          A03_02_CopyData has already wiped live A03 data and imported the
          full A02 data tree with packages and names remapped. This task
          does not copy, delete, or recreate DocSet, Pages, or PageGroups.
          Do not read leftover trees such as data_IGNORE. Do not read
          BmlDocSetPlan as the identity source. Do not invent pages that
          are not in BmlDocSet_A03.pages. Do not edit A02. Do not write
          Pages outside a03.

          Use org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
          only as a structural template (member shape, content roles,
          how sources bind to annotations). Do not copy its domain claims
          onto other pages. Keep the imported page identity (is, isNot,
          title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType, lib see-links). Existing
          semantic scaffold on an imported page is never authoritative:
          discard learningObjectives, readerOutcomes, scopes, exclusions,
          page-level authoritativeSources, and content, then regenerate
          them. Keep the FQN / file path so the same Block is updated.

          1. Read the imported A03 pages
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03.
          Walk BmlDocSet_A03.pages in listed order. For each listed A03
          DocPage, inspect is, isNot, documentation, references/see, title,
          purpose, detailLevel, and pageType. Those identity fields stay.
          Also note BmlDocSet_A03.homePage and, on each A03 PageGroup,
          pages and landingPage — this task does not rebuild those slots.

          2. Open the authoritative sources
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type
          for each selector on org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source.BlockMLSourceSet).
          That set is the same whitelist as A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons:
          org.blockml.bml.constraint.**, org.blockml.bml.core.**,
          org.blockml.bml.definition.**, org.blockml.bml.documentation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.exception.**, org.blockml.bml.group.**,
          org.blockml.bml.language.**, org.blockml.bml.mapping.**,
          org.blockml.bml.meta.**, org.blockml.bml.relation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.service.**, org.blockml.bml.status.**,
          org.blockml.bml.type.**, org.blockml.bml.unit.**,
          org.blockml.bml.validation.**.

          Those lib Blocks are the only non-A03 Blocks an A03 page may
          reference (see, authoritativeSources, annotation sources). Never
          link a Block from another sector (a01, a02, a04, or any later
          sector). Never keep an A02 page or PageGroup FQN on an A03 page.
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.** (for example BlockMLSourceSet and
          lib rules) may also be referenced. Docgen types
          (org.blockml.bml.docgen.**) may appear as structural see-links
          (for example Navigation on an Index page), not as sector content.

          For each candidate source, inspect is, documentation, and
          references — do not guess from the FQN alone.

          3. Bind sources and author the semantic specification
          For each A03 page, start from the imported purpose, title, and
          see links. From the Blocks allowed by step 2, select the SSOT
          Blocks that actually cover that purpose. Those selected Blocks
          are the page's authoritative sources. Every content page must
          have at least one Requires see-link to a lib SSOT Block. If
          several match, Requires = primary SSOT; SeeAlso = supporting
          background. Do not attach a source that does not serve the
          purpose.

          Then enrich the page after the pattern of PageExample_A03.
          Inspect that example, then inspect the DocPage / ContentElement /
          semantic types. Each authored page must:

          - declare page-level authoritativeSources as an
            AuthorativeSourceSet whose includedTypes are the bound lib
            SSOT FQNs (not sector FQNs)
          - author learningObjectives, readerOutcomes, scopes, and
            exclusions as owned semantic instances (summary + optional
            authoritativeSources / reason), grounded in the bound sources
            and the imported purpose — not copied from PageExample_A03
          - author content as an ordered semantic scaffold: Section
            (heading + purpose + nested content) and ContentElements
            (Paragraph, List, ListItem, CodeBlock, Navigation as needed)
          - on each ContentElement set purpose, message, role
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.role.*), detailLevel
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*), and weight
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.weight.*)
          - attach supportingPoints and exclusions on elements when they
            sharpen the claim; bind their authoritativeSources to lib
            Blocks from step 2
          - omit CodeBlock.code — A04 generates the listing from message,
            supportingPoints, exclusions, and authoritativeSources
          - omit finished reader-facing article prose, HTML, and filled
            example bodies; message states the claim to convey, purpose
            states why the element exists for the renderer
          - for pageType Index (for example TableOfContents): author a
            Navigation tree whose NavigationItem targets are A03 pages
            only (from BmlDocSet_A03 and the A03 PageGroups). Do not
            invent conceptual body on an Index page
          - NavigationItem.target and any in-page continuation link may
            name only A03 pages listed on BmlDocSet_A03
          - never list an A02, A01, or A04 Block in see,
            authoritativeSources, annotation sources, or Navigation

          The result is a page that specifies exactly which ideas,
          sections, roles, and sources A04 must manifest — not the
          manifested page itself.

          4. Export A03 pages from the catalog
          Export each A03 page authored here from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not already in the
          catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other sectors. Do not
          remove PageExample_A03 if it is catalogued.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A03_01_AuthorPages>
